{
  "title": "14: Ibrahim ابراهيم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالۤرٰ كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ اِلَيْكَ لِتُخْرِجَ النَّاسَ مِنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ  ۙ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِۙ‏(1)\nAR-RAA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO ELAYKA LETUKHREJA NAASA MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL NOORE BE-IZNIL RABBEHIM ELAA SERAATE A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nA. L. R. A Book which We have revealed unto thee, in order that thou mightest lead mankind out of the depths of darkness into light - by the leave of their Lord - to the Way of (Him) the Exalted in power, worthy of all praise!- \nاللّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَوَيْلٌ لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مِنْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدِ ۙ‏(2)\nLAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WAYLUL LIL-KAAFEREEN MIN A’ZAABIN SHADEEDE.\nOf Allah, to Whom do belong all things in the heavens and on earth! But alas for the Unbelievers for a terrible penalty (their Unfaith will bring them)!- \nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَحِبُّوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا عَلَى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YASTAHEBBOONA HAYAATAD DUNYAA A’LAL AAKHERATE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAYABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN AOOLAAEKA FEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nThose who love the life of this world more than the Hereafter, who hinder (men) from the Path of Allah and seek therein something crooked: they are astray by a long distance. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا بِلِسَانِ قَوْمِهٖ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْؕ فَيُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(4)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA BELESAANE QAWMEHI LEEBAYNA LAHUM FA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nWe sent not a messenger except (to teach) in the language of his (own) people, in order to make (things) clear to them. Now Allah leaves straying those whom He pleases and guides whom He pleases: and He is Exalted in power, full of Wisdom. \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اَنْ اَخْرِجْ قَوْمَكَ مِنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ ۙ وَذَكِّرْهُمْ بِاَيّٰٮمِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍ‏(5)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA AN AAKHREJ QAWMAKA MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL NOORE WAZAKKERHUM BEAAYME LAAH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nWe sent Moses with Our signs (and the command). “Bring out thy people from the depths of darkness into light, and teach them to remember the Days of Allah.” Verily in this there are Signs for such as are firmly patient and constant, grateful and appreciative. \nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهِ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ اَنْجٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُوْمُوْنَكُمْ سُوْۤءَ الْعَذَابِ وَ يُذَبِّحُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُوْنَ نِسَآءَكُمْ ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ بَلَاۤ ءٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيْمٌ‏(6)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LEQAWMEHE KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ AANJAAKUM MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YASOOMOONAKUM SOOA A’ZAABE WA YOZABBEHOONA ABNAAA-AKUM WA YAS-TAHYOONA NESAAAKUM WA FEE ZAA ZAALEKUM BALAA UN MIN RABBEKUM A’ZEEM.\nRemember! Moses said to his people: “Call to mind the favour of Allah to you when He delivered you from the people of Pharaoh: they set you hard tasks and punishments, slaughtered your sons, and let your women-folk live: therein was a tremendous trial from your Lord.” \nوَاِذْ تَاَذَّنَ رَبُّكُمْ لَئِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ لَاَزِيْدَنَّكُمْ وَلَئِنْ كَفَرْتُمْ اِنَّ عَذَابِىْ لَشَدِيْدٌ‏(7)\nWA IZ TAAZZANA RABBOKUM LAIL SHAKARTUM LAAZEEDANNAKUM WA LAIN KAFARTUM INNAL A’AZAABEAA KHAYRE.\nAnd remember! your Lord caused to be declared (publicly): “If ye are grateful, I will add more (favours) unto you; But if ye show ingratitude, truly My punishment is terrible indeed.” \nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اِنْ تَكْفُرُوْۤا اَنْتُمْ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ۙ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَنِىٌّ حَمِيْدٌ‏(8)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA IN TAKFUROOA ANTUM WA MAN FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A FA-INNAL LAAHA LA-GHANIYYUN HAMEED.\nAnd Moses said: “If ye show ingratitude, ye and all on earth together, yet is Allah free of all wants, worthy of all praise. \nاَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ نَبَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ  ۛؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ ۛؕ لَا يَعْلَمُهُمْ اِلَّا اللّٰهُؕ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَرَدُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمْ فِىْۤ اَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كَفَرْنَا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ وَاِنَّا لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ مُرِيْبٍ‏(9)\nALAM YAATEKUM NABAUA LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WAL LAZEENA MIN BA’DEHIM LAA YAA’LAMUHUM ILLAA LAAH JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FARADDOOA AYDEYAHUM FEE AFWAA-HEHIM WA QAALOO INNAA KAFARNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI WA INNAA LAFEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA TADU’OONANAA ELAYHE MOREEB.\nHas not the story reached you, (O people!), of those who (went) before you? - of the people of Noah, and 'Ad, and Thamud? - And of those who (came) after them? None knows them but Allah. To them came messengers with Clear (Signs); but they put their hands up to their mouths, and said: “We do deny (the mission) on which ye have been sent, and we are really in suspicious (disquieting) doubt as to that to which ye invite us.” \nقَالَتْ رُسُلُهُمْ اَفِى اللّٰهِ شَكٌّ فَاطِرِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يَدْعُوْكُمْ لِيَغْفِرَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُنُوْبِكُمْ وَيُؤَخِّرَكُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَاؕ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَصُدُّوْنَا عَمَّا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا فَاْتُوْنَا بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(10)\nQAALAT JAAA-ATHUM AAFEAA LAAHE SHAKKUN FAATERE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ YADU’OOKUM LEEGHFERA LAKUM MIN ZUNOOBEKUM WAYUAKKHERAKUM ELAA ELAA MOSAMMAA QAALOO IN ANTUM ILLAA BASHARUM MMESLUNAA TOREEDOONA AN TASUDDOONAA A’MMAA KAANA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA FAATOONAA BESULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nTheir messengers said: “Is there a doubt about Allah, The Creator of the heavens and the earth? It is He Who invites you, in order that He may forgive you your sins and give you respite for a term appointed!” They said: “Ah! ye are no more than human, like ourselves! Ye wish to turn us away from the (gods) our fathers used to worship: then bring us some clear authority.” \nقَالَتْ لَهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ اِنْ نَّحْنُ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَمُنُّ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖؕ وَمَا كَانَ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّاْتِيَكُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(11)\nQAALAT LAHUM JAAA-ATHUM IN NNAHNU ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAMUNNU A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’EBAADEH WA MAA KAANA LANAA AN NNAATEEKUM BESULTAANIM ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nTheir messengers said to them: “True, we are human like yourselves, but Allah doth grant His grace to such of his servants as He pleases. It is not for us to bring you an authority except as Allah permits. And on Allah let all men of faith put their trust. \nوَمَا لَنَاۤ اَلَّا نَتَوَكَّلَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَقَدْ هَدٰٮنَا سُبُلَنَاؕ وَلَنَصْبِرَنَّ عَلٰى مَاۤ اٰذَيْتُمُوْنَاؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA MAA LANAA ALLAA NATAWAKKALA A’LAL LAAHE WA QAD HADAANAA SUBULANAA WALANASBERANNA A’LAA MAA AAAZAYTUMOONAA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\n“No reason have we why we should not put our trust on Allah. Indeed He Has guided us to the Ways we (follow). We shall certainly bear with patience all the hurt you may cause us. For those who put their trust should put their trust on Allah.” \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِرُسُلِهِمْ لَنُخْرِجَنَّكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِنَاۤ اَوْ لَتَعُوْدُنَّ فِىْ مِلَّتِنَا ؕ فَاَوْحٰۤى اِلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ لَنُهْلِكَنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(13)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LERUSULEHEM LANUKHREJANNAKUM MIN ARZENAA AW LATAU’OODUNNA FEE MELLATENAA FAAWHAA ELAYHIM RABBOHUM LANUHLEKANNA ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd the Unbelievers said to their messengers: “Be sure we shall drive you out of our land, or ye shall return to our religion.” But their Lord inspired (this Message) to them: “Verily We shall cause the wrong-doers to perish! \nوَلَنُسْكِنَنَّكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ خَافَ مَقَامِىْ وَخَافَ وَعِيْدِ‏(14)\nWALANUSKENANNAKUMU ARZA MIN BAA’DEHEM ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y KHAAFA MAQAAMEAA WA KHAAFA WAE’EEDE.\n“And verily We shall cause you to abide in the land, and succeed them. This for such as fear the Time when they shall stand before My tribunal, such as fear the punishment denounced.” \nوَاسْتَفْتَحُوْا وَخَابَ كُلُّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍۙ‏(15)\nWAASTAFTAHOOA WA QAD KULLO JABBAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\nBut they sought victory and decision (there and then), and frustration was the lot of every powerful obstinate transgressor. \nمِّنْ وَّرَآئِهٖ جَهَنَّمُ وَيُسْقٰى مِنْ مَّآءٍ صَدِيْدٍۙ‏(16)\nMIN WWARAAEH JAHANNAMUL WAYUSQAA MIN MAAA-IN SADEEDIN.\nIn front of such a one is Hell, and he is given, for drink, boiling fetid water. \nيَّتَجَرَّعُهٗ وَلَا يَكَادُ يُسِيْغُهٗ وَيَاْتِيْهِ الْمَوْتُ مِنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ وَّمَا هُوَ بِمَيِّتٍؕ وَمِنْ وَّرَآئِهٖ عَذَابٌ غَلِيْظٌ‏(17)\nYYATAJARRAU’UH WA LAA YAKAADUL YUSEEGHUH WA YAATEEHIL MAWTO MIN KULLE MAKAANIN WA MAA HOWA BEMAYTIN WA MIN WWARAAEH A’ZAABUN GHALEEZUN.\nIn gulps will he sip it, but never will he be near swallowing it down his throat: death will come to him from every quarter, yet will he not die: and in front of him will be a chastisement unrelenting. \nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ كَرَمَادِ ۨاشْتَدَّتْ بِهِ الرِّيْحُ فِىْ يَوْمٍ عَاصِفٍؕ لَا يَقْدِرُوْنَ مِمَّا كَسَبُوْا عَلٰى شَىْءٍؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الضَّلٰلُ الْبَعِيْدُ‏(18)\nMASALUL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM A-A’MAALOHUM KARAMAADE ASHTADDAT BEHIL AR-REEHU FEE YAWMIN A’AASEFIN LAA YAQDEROONA MIMMAA KASABOO A’LAA SHAYIN ZAA LEKA HOWA AZ-ZALAALU AL-BAE’EEDU.\nThe parable of those who reject their Lord is that their works are as ashes, on which the wind blows furiously on a tempestuous day: No power have they over aught that they have earned: that is the straying far, far (from the goal). \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ وَيَاْتِ بِخَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍۙ‏(19)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ IN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM WA TAKOONOO BE-KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nSeest thou not that Allah created the heavens and the earth in Truth? If He so will, He can remove you and put (in your place) a new creation? \nوَّمَا ذٰلِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(20)\nWA MAA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE BEA’AZEEZIN.\nNor is that for Allah any great matter. \nوَبَرَزُوْا لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا فَقَالَ الضُّعَفٰۤؤُا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمْ تَبَعًا فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّغْنُوْنَ عَنَّا مِنْ عَذَابِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ قَالُوْا لَوْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ لَهَدَيْنٰكُمْؕ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَجَزِعْنَاۤ اَمْ صَبَرْنَا مَا لَنَا مِنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(21)\nWA BARAZOO LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A FAQAALA AZ-ZUA’AFAAUA LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KUNNAA LAKUM TABAA’AN FA HAL ANTUM MMUGHNOONA WAGH MIN A’ZAABIN LAAHE MIN SHAYIN QAALOO LAW HADAANAA LAAHO LAHADAYNAAKUM SAWAAA-UN A’LAYNAA AAJAZEA’NAA AM SABARNAA MAA LANAA MIN MAHEES.\nThey will all be marshalled before Allah together: then will the weak say to those who were arrogant, “For us, we but followed you; can ye then avail us to all against the wrath of Allah?” They will reply, “If we had received the Guidance of Allah, we should have given it to you: to us it makes no difference (now) whether we rage, or bear (these torments) with patience: for ourselves there is no way of escape.” \nوَقَالَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لَمَّا قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ وَعَدَكُمْ وَعْدَ الْحَقِّ وَوَعَدْتُّكُمْ فَاَخْلَفْتُكُمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِىَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ دَعَوْتُكُمْ فَاسْتَجَبْتُمْ لِىْ ۚ فَلَا تَلُوْمُوْنِىْ وَلُوْمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ ؕ مَاۤ اَنَا بِمُصْرِخِكُمْ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُصْرِخِىَّ ؕ اِنِّىْ كَفَرْتُ بِمَاۤ اَشْرَكْتُمُوْنِ مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(22)\nWA QAALA SHAYTAANO LAMMAA QUZEAAA MIN INNAL LAAHA WAA’ADAKUM WA’DAL HAQQE WAWAA’ADTTUKUM FAAKHLAFTUKUM WA MAA KAANA LEYA A’LAYKUM MIN SULTAANIN ILLAA AN DAA’AWTUKUM FAASTAJABTUM LEE FALAA TALOOMOONEAA WALOOMOOA ANFOSAKUM MAA ANAA BEMUSREKHEKUM WA MAA ANTUM BEMUSREKHEAAAA INNEE KAFARTU BEMAA AASHRAKTUMOONE MIN QABLO INNAL ZAALEMEEN LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAnd Satan will say when the matter is decided: “It was Allah Who gave you a promise of Truth: I too promised, but I failed in my promise to you. I had no authority over you except to call you but ye listened to me: then reproach not me, but reproach your own souls. I cannot listen to your cries, nor can ye listen to mine. I reject your former act in associating me with Allah. For wrong-doers there must be a grievous penalty.” \nوَاُدْخِلَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِمْؕ تَحِيَّتُهُمْ فِيْهَا سَلٰمٌ‏(23)\nWAADKHELA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA BE-IZNIL RABBEHIM TAHIYYATOHUM FEEHAA SALAAMUN.\nBut those who believe and work righteousness will be admitted to gardens beneath which rivers flow, to dwell therein for aye with the leave of their Lord. Their greeting therein will be: “Peace!” \nاَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ ضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا كَلِمَةً طَيِّبَةً كَشَجَرَةٍ طَيِّبَةٍ اَصْلُهَا ثَابِتٌ وَّفَرْعُهَا فِى السَّمَآءِۙ‏(24)\nALAM TARA KAYFA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA KALEMATAN TAYBATAN KASHAJARATIN TAYBATIN AASLUHAA SAABETUN WWAFARU’UHAA FIL SAMAAA-E.\nSeest thou not how Allah sets forth a parable? - A goodly word like a goodly tree, whose root is firmly fixed, and its branches (reach) to the heavens, of its Lord. So Allah sets forth parables for men, in order that they may receive admonition. \nتُؤْتِىْۤ اُكُلَهَا كُلَّ حِيْنٍۢ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهَاؕ وَيَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْاَمْثَالَ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(25)\nTUTEAA OKOLAHAA KULLA HEEN BE-IZNIL RABBEHAA WAYAZREBU LAAHO AL-AAMSAALA LIN-NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nIt brings forth its fruit at all times, by the leave of its Lord. So Allah sets forth parables for men, in order that they may receive admonition. \nوَمَثَلُ كَلِمَةٍ خَبِيْثَةٍ كَشَجَرَةٍ خَبِيْثَةٍۨاجْتُثَّتْ مِنْ فَوْقِ الْاَرْضِ مَا لَهَا مِنْ قَرَارٍ‏(26)\nWA MASALUL KALEMATIN KHABEESATIN KASHAJARATIN KHABEESATINAJTUSSAT MIN FAWQE ARZE MAA LAHAA MIN QARAARIN.\nAnd the parable of an evil Word is that of an evil tree: It is torn up by the root from the surface of the earth: it has no stability. \nيُثَبِّتُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِالْقَوْلِ الثَّابِتِ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَيُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ ۙ وَيَفْعَلُ اللّٰهُ مَا يَشَآءُ‏(27)\nYUSABBETU LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-QAWLE AS-SAABETE FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA AAKHERATE WA YOZILLO LAAHO ZAALEMEEN WA YAF-A’LO LAAHO MAA YASHAAA.\nAllah will establish in strength those who believe, with the word that stands firm, in this world and in the Hereafter; but Allah will leave, to stray, those who do wrong: Allah doeth what He willeth. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ بَدَّلُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ كُفْرًا وَّاَحَلُّوْا قَوْمَهُمْ دَارَ الْبَوَارِۙ‏(28)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA BADDALOO NEA’MATAL LAAHE KUFRAN WWAAHALLOOA QAWMAHUM DAARA AL-BAWAARE.\nHast thou not turned thy vision to those who have changed the favour of Allah. Into blasphemy and caused their people to descend to the House of Perdition? \nجَهَنَّمَۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَاؕ وَبِئْسَ الْقَرَارُ‏(29)\nJAHANNAMA YASLAWNAHAA WA BEASAL AL-QARAARU.\nInto Hell? They will burn therein, an evil place to stay in! \nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا لِّيُضِلُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖؕ قُلْ تَمَتَّعُوْا فَاِنَّ مَصِيْرَكُمْ اِلَى النَّارِ‏(30)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE ANDAADANW LLEEZELLOOA A’N SABEELEH QUL TAMATTAU’OOA FA-INNAL MASEERAKUM ELAL NAAR.\nAnd they set up (idols) as equal to Allah, to mislead (men) from the Path! Say: “Enjoy (your brief power)! But verily ye are making straightway for Hell!” \nقُلْ لِّعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يُقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُنْفِقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ يَوْمٌ لَّا بَيْعٌ فِيْهِ وَلَا خِلٰلٌ‏(31)\nQUL LLEE’EBAADEAAA LAZEENA AAMANOO YUQEEMOOA SALAATA WAYUNFEQOOA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM SIRRAN WA A’LAANEYATAN MIN QABLE AN YAATEYA YAWMUL LAA BAY-U’N FEEHE WA LAA KHELAALUN.\nSpeak to my servants who have believed, that they may establish regular prayers, and spend (in charity) out of the sustenance we have given them, secretly and openly, before the coming of a Day in which there will be neither mutual bargaining nor befriending. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَاَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَخْرَجَ بِهٖ مِنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْفُلْكَ لِتَجْرِىَ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِاَمْرِهٖۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْاَنْهٰرَۚ‏(32)\nALLAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ANZALA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AKHRAJA BEHI MENAL SAMARAATE RIZQAN LAKUM SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL AL-FULKA LETAJREAAA FIL BAHRE LAAHO SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL AL-AANHAARA.\nIt is Allah Who hath created the heavens and the earth and sendeth down rain from the skies, and with it bringeth out fruits wherewith to feed you; it is He Who hath made the ships subject to you, that they may sail through the sea by His command; and the rivers (also) hath He made subject to you. \nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ دَآئِبَيْنِۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَۚ‏(33)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL SHAMSA WAL QAMARA DAAEBAYNE SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA.\nAnd He hath made subject to you the sun and the moon, both diligently pursuing their courses; and the night and the day hath he (also) made subject to you. \nوَاٰتٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ مَا سَاَلْتُمُوْهُ ؕ وَاِنْ تَعُدُّوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ لَا تُحْصُوْهَا ؕ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَظَلُوْمٌ كَفَّارٌ‏(34)\nWA AATAAKUM MIN KULLE MAA SAALTUMOOHU WA TAU’UDDOOA NEA’MATAL LAAHE LAA TUHSOOHAA INNAL INSAANA LAZALOOMUN KAFFAARUN.\nAnd He giveth you of all that ye ask for. But if ye count the favours of Allah, never will ye be able to number them. Verily, man is given up to injustice and ingratitude. \nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هٰذَا الْبَلَدَ اٰمِنًا وَّاجْنُبْنِىْ وَبَنِىَّ اَنْ نَّعْبُدَ الْاَصْنَامَؕ‏(35)\nWA IZ QAALA AEBRAAHEEMU RABBE A’L HAAZAA AL-BALADA AAMENANW WWAAJNUBNEAA WABANEAAAA AN NNAA’BUDA AL-AASNAAMA.\nRemember Abraham said: “O my Lord! make this city one of peace and security: and preserve me and my sons from worshipping idols. \nرَبِّ اِنَّهُنَّ اَضْلَلْنَ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِۚ فَمَنْ تَبِعَنِىْ فَاِنَّهٗ مِنِّىْۚ وَمَنْ عَصَانِىْ فَاِنَّكَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(36)\nRABBE AENNAHUNNA AAZLALNA KASEERAA MENAL NAASE FAMAN TABEA’ANEAA FA-INNAHU MINNEE WA MAN A’ASAANEAA FA-INNAKA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\n“O my Lord! they have indeed led astray many among mankind; He then who follows my (ways) is of me, and he that disobeys me, but Thou art indeed Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْكَنْتُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِىْ زَرْعٍ عِنْدَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِۙ رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيْمُوْا الصَّلٰوةَ فَاجْعَلْ اَ فْئِدَةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ وَارْزُقْهُمْ مِّنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(37)\nRABBANAA INNEE AASKANTU MIN ZURREETEAA BEWAADIN GHAIRE ZEE ZARA’IN I’NDAL BAYTEKA AL-MUHARRAME RABBANAA LEEQEEMOOA SALAATA FAJ-A’L A’ZAABAN FEDATAN MENAL NAASE TAHWEAA ELAYHIM WAARZUQHUM MENAL SAMARAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YASHKOROON.\n“O our Lord! I have made some of my offspring to dwell in a valley without cultivation, by Thy Sacred House; in order, O our Lord, that they may establish regular Prayer: so fill the hearts of some among men with love towards them, and feed them with fruits: so that they may give thanks. \nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ تَعْلَمُ مَا نُخْفِىْ وَمَا نُعْلِنُ ؕ وَمَا يَخْفٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ‏(38)\nRABBANAA INNAKA TAA’LAMU MAA NUKHFEAA WA MAA NUA’LENU WA MAA YAKHFAA A’LAL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN FIL ARZE WA LAA FIL SAMAAA-E.\n“O our Lord! truly Thou dost know what we conceal and what we reveal: for nothing whatever is hidden from Allah, whether on earth or in heaven. \nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ وَهَبَ لِىْ عَلَى الْكِبَرِ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَسَمِيْعُ الدُّعَآءِ‏(39)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE WAHABA LEE A’LAL AL-KEBARE AESMAAE’EELA WAASHAAQA INNAL RABBEE LASAMEEU’U AD-DUA’AAE.\n“Praise be to Allah, Who hath granted unto me in old age Isma'il and Isaac: for truly my Lord is He, the Hearer of Prayer! \nرَبِّ اجْعَلْنِىْ مُقِيْمَ الصَّلٰوةِ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ ۖ  رَبَّنَا وَتَقَبَّلْ دُعَآءِ‏(40)\nRABBE AJA’ALNEAA MUQEEMA AS-SALAAWTE WA MIN ZURREETEAA RABBANAA WA RABBANAA DO-A’AA-IL.\nO my Lord! make me one who establishes regular Prayer, and also (raise such) among my offspring O our Lord! and accept Thou my Prayer. \nرَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لِىْ وَلِوَالِدَىَّ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ يَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْحِسَابُ‏(41)\nRABBANAA FIR LEE WALEWAALEDAA LIL-MOAMENEENA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUL AL-HESAABU.\n“O our Lord! cover (us) with Thy Forgiveness - me, my parents, and (all) Believers, on the Day that the Reckoning will be established! \nوَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَافِلًا عَمَّا يَعْمَلُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ ؕ اِنَّمَا يُؤَخِّرُهُمْ لِيَوْمٍ تَشْخَصُ فِيْهِ الْاَبْصَارُ ۙ‏(42)\nWA LAA TAHSABANNA LAAHA GHAAFELAN A’MMAA YAA’MALU ZAALEMOON INNAMAA YUAKKHERUHUM LE-YAWMIN TASHKHASU FEEHE IZ ZAAGHATIL.\nThink not that Allah doth not heed the deeds of those who do wrong. He but giveth them respite against a Day when the eyes will fixedly stare in horror, \nمُهْطِعِيْنَ مُقْنِعِىْ رُءُوْسِهِمْ لَا يَرْتَدُّ اِلَيْهِمْ طَرْفُهُمْ ۚ وَاَفْئِدَتُهُمْ هَوَآءٌ ؕ‏(43)\nMUHTEE’EENA MUQNEE’EAA RUOOSEHEM LAA YARTADDU ELAYHIM TARFUHUM WAAFEDATUHUM HAWAAUN.\nThey running forward with necks outstretched, their heads uplifted, their gaze returning not towards them, and their hearts a (gaping) void! \nوَاَنْذِرِ النَّاسَ يَوْمَ يَاْتِيْهِمُ الْعَذَابُ فَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَخِّرْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ نُّجِبْ دَعْوَتَكَ وَنَتَّبِعِ الرُّسُلَؕ اَوَلَمْ تَكُوْنُوْۤااَقْسَمْتُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ مَالَكُمْ مِّنْ زَوَالٍۙ‏(44)\nWAANZERE NAASA YAWMA YAATEEHEMU A’ZAABO FAYAQOOLO LAZEENA ZALAMOO RABBANAA AAKKHERNAA ELAA ELAA QAREEBIN NNUJEB DAA’WATAKA WANATTABEE’E AR-RUSULA AWALAM TAKOONOOAAAQSAMTUM MIN QABLO MAALAKUM MIN ZAWAALIN.\nSo warn mankind of the Day when the Wrath will reach them: then will the wrong-doers say: “Our Lord! respite us (if only) for a short term: we will answer Thy call, and follow the messengers!” “What! were ye not wont to swear aforetime that ye should suffer no decline? \nوَّسَكَنْتُمْ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمْ كَيْفَ فَعَلْنَا بِهِمْ وَضَرَبْنَا لَكُمُ الْاَمْثَالَ‏(45)\nWWASAKANTUM FEE MASAAKENE LAZEENA ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM WA TABAYYANA LAKUM KAYFA FAA’ALNAA BEHIM WA ZARABNAA LAKOMUL AL-AAMSAALA.\n“And ye dwelt in the dwellings of men who wronged their own souls; ye were clearly shown how We dealt with them; and We put forth (many) parables in your behoof!” \nوَقَدْ مَكَرُوْا مَكْرَهُمْ وَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ مَكْرُهُمْؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مَكْرُهُمْ لِتَزُوْلَ مِنْهُ الْجِبَالُ‏(46)\nWA QAD MAKAROOA MAKRAHUM WA I’NDAL LAAHE MAKRUHUM WA KAANA MAKRUHUM LETAZOOLA MINHO JEBAALO.\nMighty indeed were the plots which they made, but their plots were (well) within the sight of Allah, even though they were such as to shake the hills! \nفَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِفَ وَعْدِهٖ رُسُلَهٗؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ ذُوْ انْتِقَامٍؕ‏(47)\nFALAA TAHSABANNA LAAHA MUKHLEFA WAA’DEH RUSULAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN ZOO ANTEQAAMIN.\nNever think that Allah would fail his messengers in His promise: for Allah is Exalted in power, - the Lord of Retribution. \nيَوْمَ تُبَدَّلُ الْاَرْضُ غَيْرَ الْاَرْضِ وَالسَّمٰوٰتُ وَبَرَزُوْا لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ‏(48)\nYAWMA TUBADDALU ARZO GHAYRA ARZE WAALSSAMAAWAATU WA BARAZOO LILLAAHE AL-WAAHEDE AL-QAHHAARE.\nOne day the earth will be changed to a different earth, and so will be the heavens, and (men) will be marshalled forth, before Allah, the One, the Irresistible; \nوَتَرَى الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ يَوْمَئِذٍ مُّقَرَّنِيْنَ فِى الْاَصْفَادِۚ‏(49)\nWA TARAL MUJREMEEN YAWMA-EZIN MMUQARRANEENA FIL AL-AASFAADE.\nAnd thou wilt see the sinners that day bound together in fetters;- \nسَرَابِيْلُهُمْ مِّنْ قَطِرَانٍ وَّتَغْشٰى وُجُوْهَهُمُ النَّارُۙ‏(50)\nSARAABEELUHUM MIN QATERAANIN WWATAGHSHAA WUJOOHAHUMU TAMASSANAN.\nTheir garments of liquid pitch, and their faces covered with Fire; \nلِيَجْزِىَ اللّٰهُ كُلَّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(51)\nLE-YAJZEYAL LAAHO KULLA NAFSIM MAA KASABAT INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThat Allah may requite each soul according to its deserts; and verily Allah is swift in calling to account. \nهٰذَا بَلٰغٌ لِّلنَّاسِ وَلِيُنْذَرُوْا بِهٖ وَلِيَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ وَّلِيَذَّكَّرَ اُولُوا الْا َلْبَابِ‏(52)\nHAAZAA BALAAGHUN LIN-NAASE WALEENZAROOA BEHI WALEEA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED WWALEEZZAKKARA ULUL AL-A LBAABE.\nHere is a Message for mankind: Let them take warning therefrom, and let them know that He is (no other than) One Allah: let men of understanding take heed. ",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah that has 52 verses. It is narrated by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah Ibrahim and [Surah Hijr](A19) in a two-rak’aat prayer on every Friday, he will remain safe from poverty, insanity and sudden calamity.\nIn Tafseer al-Burhan, it is mentioned that writing this Surah on a white parchment and then making a child wear it as a talisman keeps the child safe from ailments and makes it easy for him to drink and digest milk."
}
